IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa18-part22-interest`

-- coa18-part22-notice.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 22 (information about interests in a company's
-- shares), ss 791 to 807: who the Part applies to, the notice requiring information, orders imposing restrictions,
-- the members' power to require the company to act, and the report to members. Lines 10757-10932 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively. The seat layer is coa18-seat.l4.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are generated by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the provision (an offence is committed, a power is given ...).
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("only", "if", "where", "unless", a flat negative, a fixed
--               period that has run out). Each such branch carries  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, or limited by its own wording. Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--
-- THE GATE OF s 791. "This Part applies only to public companies." The functions below answer on the footing that the
-- Part applies; `s 791 this Part applies to the company` answers whether it does, and a caller (the seat layer) puts the
-- two together. Gating every function would repeat one rule thirty times.
--
-- SEAMS (taken as inputs, never imported): `s 4(2) the company is a public company` (BOOLEAN); `s 1121 the officer is
-- in default` (MAYBE BOOLEAN: NOTHING stays NOTHING); `s 1136 ...` (place specified in regulations).
--
-- PERIODS. s 827 reckons a period expressed as a number of days in working days (module coa18-part22-interest, which this module
-- imports). The duties below that carry such a period take the count of working days elapsed as a plain input, and each has a
-- companion function giving the last day of the period through s 827's stepper.

§ `Part 22 (ss 791 to 828), first module: ss 791 to 807`

§§ `s 791 Companies to which this Part applies`

-- src:10759 | 791 Companies to which this Part applies
-- src:10760 | This Part applies only to public companies.
@ref s 791 Companies to which this Part applies (src:10759-10760)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 791 this Part applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This Part applies only to public companies."

§§ `s 792 Shares to which this Part applies`

-- (1) A closed definition ("References ... are to ..."): the issued shares of a voting class, treasury shares included.
-- src:10762 | (1) References in this Part to a company's shares are to the company's issued shares of a class carrying rights to vote in all circumstances at general meetings of the company (including any shares held as treasury shares).
@ref s 792(1) Shares to which this Part applies (src:10762-10762)
GIVEN `the shares are issued shares of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are of a class carrying rights to vote in all circumstances at general meetings of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 792(1) the shares are the company's shares for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF     `the shares are of a class carrying rights to vote in all circumstances at general meetings of the company`
       AND (   `the shares are issued shares of the company`
            OR `the shares are held as treasury shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "References in this Part to a company's shares are to the company's issued shares of a class carrying rights to vote in all circumstances at general meetings of the company (including any shares held as treasury shares)."

-- src:10763 | (2) The temporary suspension of voting rights in respect of any shares does not affect the application of this Part in relation to interests in those or any other shares.
@ref s 792(2) Shares to which this Part applies (src:10763-10763)
GIVEN `the suspension of voting rights is temporary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 792(2) a suspension of voting rights affects the application of this Part to interests in those or any other shares` MEANS
    IF `the suspension of voting rights is temporary`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The temporary suspension of voting rights in respect of any shares does not affect the application of this Part in relation to interests in those or any other shares."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The temporary suspension of voting rights": a suspension that is not temporary is not mentioned

§§ `s 793 Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares`

-- src:10766 | (1) A public company may give notice under this section to any person whom the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe—
-- src:10767 | (a) to be interested in the company's shares, or
-- src:10768 | (b) to have been so interested at any time during the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued.
@ref s 793(1) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10766-10768)
GIVEN `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the person is interested in the company's shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the person was so interested at some time during the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` MEANS
    IF     `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the person is interested in the company's shares`
        OR `the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe that the person was so interested at some time during the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to any person whom the company knows or has reasonable cause to believe": the grant names whom; it does not forbid the rest

-- (1)(b): the three years run from three years before the notice date up to, but not including, the notice date
-- (a present interest on the notice date itself is limb (a)). The period is fixed in the text's own words.
@ref s 793(1)(b) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10768-10768)
GIVEN `the date on which the person was interested` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(1)(b) the date is within the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued` MEANS
    IF     Day (`add years` `the date on which the notice is issued` (0 MINUS 3)) AT MOST Day `the date on which the person was interested`
       AND Day `the date on which the person was interested` LESS THAN Day `the date on which the notice is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time during the three years immediately preceding the date on which the notice is issued"

-- (2)(a): a notice the company may give under (1) may require the person to confirm the fact or state whether or not.
-- src:10769 | (2) The notice may require the person—
-- src:10770 | (a) to confirm that fact or (as the case may be) to state whether or not it is the case, and
-- src:10771 | (b) if he holds, or has during that time held, any such interest, to give such further information as may be required in accordance with the following provisions of this section.
@ref s 793(2) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10769-10771)
GIVEN `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(2)(a) the notice may require the person to confirm that fact or to state whether or not it is the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 793(1) the company may give notice to the person`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice may require the person" refers to a notice under this section; if the company may not give one the text says nothing

@ref s 793(2)(b) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10771-10771)
GIVEN `the person holds, or has during that time held, an interest in the company's shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(2)(b) the notice may require the person to give further information` MEANS
    IF `the person holds, or has during that time held, an interest in the company's shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) if he holds, or has during that time held, any such interest, to give such further information": a grant gated by if; the text is silent on the case where the gate fails (fork F42)

-- src:10772 | (3) The notice may require the person to whom it is addressed to give particulars of his own present or past interest in the company's shares (held by him at any time during the three year period mentioned in subsection (1)(b)).
@ref s 793(3) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10772-10772)
GIVEN `the person held the interest at some time during the three year period mentioned in subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(3) the notice may require the person to give particulars of his own present or past interest` MEANS
    IF `the person held the interest at some time during the three year period mentioned in subsection (1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(held by him at any time during the three year period mentioned in subsection (1)(b))": an interest outside the period is not mentioned

-- src:10773 | (4) The notice may require the person to whom it is addressed, where—
-- src:10774 | (a) his interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists, or
-- src:10775 | (b) another interest in the shares subsisted during that three year period at a time when his interest subsisted,
-- src:10776 | to give, so far as lies within his knowledge, such particulars with respect to that other interest as may be required by the notice.
@ref s 793(4) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10773-10776)
GIVEN `the person's interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another interest in the shares subsisted during that three year period at a time when the person's interest subsisted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(4) the notice may require the person to give such particulars with respect to that other interest as the notice requires` MEANS
    IF     `the person's interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists`
        OR `another interest in the shares subsisted during that three year period at a time when the person's interest subsisted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice may require the person to whom it is addressed, where— (a) his interest is a present interest and another interest in the shares subsists, or (b) another interest in the shares subsisted during that three year period at a time when his interest subsisted"

DECLARE `s 793(5) kind of particular` IS ONE OF
    `s 793(5)(a) the identity of persons interested in the shares in question`
    `s 793(5)(b)(i) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement to which section 824 applies`
    `s 793(5)(b)(ii) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement or arrangement relating to the exercise of any rights conferred by the holding of the shares`
    `s 793(5) another kind of particular`

-- src:10777 | (5) The particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include—
-- src:10778 | (a) the identity of persons interested in the shares in question, and
-- src:10779 | (b) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to—
-- src:10780 | (i) an agreement to which section 824 applies (certain share acquisition agreements), or
-- src:10781 | (ii) an agreement or arrangement relating to the exercise of any rights conferred by the holding of the shares.
@ref s 793(5) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10777-10781)
GIVEN `the particulars are those referred to in subsections (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 793(5) kind of particular`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(5) the particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include` MEANS
    IF `the particulars are those referred to in subsections (3) and (4)`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 793(5)(a) the identity of persons interested in the shares in question` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 793(5)(b)(i) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement to which section 824 applies` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 793(5)(b)(ii) whether persons interested in the same shares are or were parties to an agreement or arrangement relating to the exercise of any rights conferred by the holding of the shares` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4) include" does not close the list
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The particulars referred to in subsections (3) and (4)"

-- src:10782 | (6) The notice may require the person to whom it is addressed, where his interest is a past interest, to give (so far as lies within his knowledge) particulars of the identity of the person who held that interest immediately upon his ceasing to hold it.
@ref s 793(6) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10782-10782)
GIVEN `the person's interest is a past interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(6) the notice may require the person to give particulars of the identity of the person who held that interest immediately upon his ceasing to hold it` MEANS
    IF `the person's interest is a past interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where his interest is a past interest"

-- (7): the time is whatever reasonable time the notice specifies. Whether the time specified is reasonable is a
-- judgment the text leaves open, so it is an input; a time that is not reasonable is not covered.
-- src:10783 | (7) The information required by the notice must be given within such reasonable time as may be specified in the notice.
@ref s 793(7) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10783-10783)
GIVEN `the time specified in the notice is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day for giving the information specified in the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the information was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 793(7) the information required by the notice was given within the time specified` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the time specified in the notice is reasonable`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "within such reasonable time as may be specified in the notice"
        IF Day `the date on which the information was given` AT MOST Day `the last day for giving the information specified in the notice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information required by the notice must be given within such reasonable time as may be specified in the notice."

-- (7) as a duty: the person to whom the notice is addressed is not one of the core's parties, so the party and the
-- action are declared here under this section's label.
DECLARE `s 793(7) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 793(7) the person to whom the notice is addressed`

DECLARE `s 793(7) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 793(7) give the information required by the notice`

@ref s 793(7) Notice by company requiring information about interests in its shares (src:10783-10783)
GIVEN `the number of days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 793(7) party` `s 793(7) action`
`s 793(7) the person addressed must give the information required by the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 793(7) the person to whom the notice is addressed`
    MUST `s 793(7) give the information required by the notice`
    WITHIN `the number of days the notice allows`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 793(7) the person to whom the notice is addressed` BECAUSE "s 793(7): the information was not given within the time specified in the notice"

§§ `s 794 Notice requiring information: order imposing restrictions on shares`

-- (1): "Where (a) ... and (b) ..., the company may apply to the court": a "where" condition.
-- src:10785 | (1) Where—
-- src:10786 | (a) a notice under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares) is served by a company on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company, and
-- src:10787 | (b) that person fails to give the company the information required by the notice within the time specified in it,
-- src:10788 | the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions.
-- src:10789 | For the effect of such an order see section 797.
@ref s 794(1) Notice requiring information: order imposing restrictions on shares (src:10785-10789)
GIVEN `a notice under section 793 was served by the company on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person fails to give the company the information required by the notice within the time specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 794(1) the company may apply to the court for an order directing that the shares in question be subject to restrictions` MEANS
    IF     `a notice under section 793 was served by the company on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company`
       AND `that person fails to give the company the information required by the notice within the time specified in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a notice under section 793 ... is served by a company on a person who is or was interested in shares in the company, and (b) that person fails to give the company the information required by the notice within the time specified in it, the company may apply to the court"

-- (2): whether the court is satisfied is the court's judgment, so it is an input.
-- src:10790 | (2) If the court is satisfied that such an order may unfairly affect the rights of third parties in respect of the shares, the court may, for the purpose of protecting those rights and subject to such terms as it thinks fit, direct that such acts by such persons or descriptions of persons and for such purposes as may be set out in the order shall not constitute a breach of the restrictions.
@ref s 794(2) Notice requiring information: order imposing restrictions on shares (src:10790-10790)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that such an order may unfairly affect the rights of third parties in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 794(2) the court may direct that acts set out in the order shall not constitute a breach of the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that such an order may unfairly affect the rights of third parties in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied that such an order may unfairly affect the rights of third parties in respect of the shares, the court may": a grant gated by if; the text is silent on the case where the gate fails (fork F43)

-- (3): on an application the court may make an interim order, unconditionally or on such terms as it thinks fit.
-- src:10791 | (3) On an application under this section the court may make an interim order.
-- src:10792 | Any such order may be made unconditionally or on such terms as the court thinks fit.
@ref s 794(3) Notice requiring information: order imposing restrictions on shares (src:10791-10792)
GIVEN `an application has been made under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 794(3) the court may make an interim order` MEANS
    IF `an application has been made under section 794`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On an application under this section the court may make an interim order."

DECLARE `s 794(3) way of making an interim order` IS ONE OF
    `s 794(3) unconditionally`
    `s 794(3) on such terms as the court thinks fit`
    `s 794(3) in another way`

@ref s 794(3) Notice requiring information: order imposing restrictions on shares (src:10792-10792)
GIVEN way IS A `s 794(3) way of making an interim order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 794(3) the interim order may be made in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `s 794(3) unconditionally` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 794(3) on such terms as the court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Any such order may be made unconditionally or on such terms as the court thinks fit." names two ways and says nothing of a third

§§ `s 795 Notice requiring information: offences`

-- src:10795 | (1) A person who—
-- src:10796 | (a) fails to comply with a notice under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares), or
-- src:10797 | (b) in purported compliance with such a notice—
-- src:10798 | (i) makes a statement that he knows to be false in a material particular, or
-- src:10799 | (ii) recklessly makes a statement that is false in a material particular,
-- src:10800 | commits an offence.
-- src:10801 | (2) A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1)(a) if he proves that the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 795(1)(a) and (2) Notice requiring information: offences (src:10795-10801)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with a notice under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person proves that the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 795(1)(a) the person commits an offence by failing to comply with the notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person fails to comply with a notice under section 793`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who— (a) fails to comply with a notice under section 793 ... commits an offence": the offence is limited to a person who fails; a person who complied is not mentioned
        IF `the person proves that the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under subsection (1)(a) if he proves that the requirement to give information was frivolous or vexatious."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 795(1)(b) Notice requiring information: offences (src:10797-10800)
GIVEN `the person makes a statement in purported compliance with such a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows the statement to be false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person recklessly makes a statement that is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 795(1)(b) the person commits an offence by a false statement in purported compliance with the notice` MEANS
    IF     `the person makes a statement in purported compliance with such a notice`
       AND (   `the person knows the statement to be false in a material particular`
            OR `the person recklessly makes a statement that is false in a material particular`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who— ... (b) in purported compliance with such a notice— (i) makes a statement that he knows to be false in a material particular, or (ii) recklessly makes a statement that is false in a material particular, commits an offence": a person who made no such statement is not mentioned

-- (2) is inside (1)(a) above: the defence is an input there.

-- (3): the penalty by the place and manner of conviction. "on summary conviction" without a place is not covered:
-- the text divides it by place.
-- src:10802 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:10803 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:10804 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:10805 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:10806 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 795(3) Notice requiring information: offences (src:10802-10806)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 795(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding,   fine not exceeding,                                   daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment`                    THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`,                    JUST (Period OF 2, Years),   JUST `a fine without a stated limit`,                  NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`     THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`,     JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`              THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,              JUST (Period OF 6, Months),  JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,      JUST (Period OF 6, Months),  JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) on summary conviction— (i) in England and Wales ... (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland": summary conviction is divided by place

§§ `s 796 Notice requiring information: persons exempted from obligation to comply`

-- src:10808 | (1) A person is not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares) if he is for the time being exempted by the Secretary of State from the operation of that section.
@ref s 796(1) Notice requiring information: persons exempted from obligation to comply (src:10808-10808)
GIVEN `the person is for the time being exempted by the Secretary of State from the operation of section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 796(1) the person is not obliged to comply with a notice under section 793` MEANS
    IF `the person is for the time being exempted by the Secretary of State from the operation of section 793`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he is for the time being exempted": the text names the exemption as the ground; whether a person is otherwise obliged is s 793(7)

-- (2): "must not grant ... unless": the bar. Both conditions met means the bar does not apply (an "unless" met: see
-- the fork register).
-- src:10809 | (2) The Secretary of State must not grant any such exemption unless—
-- src:10810 | (a) he has consulted the Governor of the Bank of England, and
-- src:10811 | (b) he (the Secretary of State) is satisfied that, having regard to any undertaking given by the person in question with respect to any interest held or to be held by him in any shares, there are special reasons why that person should not be subject to the obligations imposed by that section.
@ref s 796(2) Notice requiring information: persons exempted from obligation to comply (src:10809-10811)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has consulted the Governor of the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, having regard to any undertaking given by the person with respect to any interest held or to be held by him in any shares, there are special reasons why that person should not be subject to the obligations imposed by section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 796(2) the Secretary of State is barred from granting the exemption` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State has consulted the Governor of the Bank of England`
       AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, having regard to any undertaking given by the person with respect to any interest held or to be held by him in any shares, there are special reasons why that person should not be subject to the obligations imposed by section 793`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary of State must not grant any such exemption unless— (a) he has consulted ... and (b) he ... is satisfied": both conditions met, so the bar does not apply
    ELSE JUST TRUE

GIVEN `the Secretary of State has consulted the Governor of the Bank of England` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, having regard to any undertaking given by the person with respect to any interest held or to be held by him in any shares, there are special reasons why that person should not be subject to the obligations imposed by section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 796(2) the Secretary of State must not grant the exemption unless the conditions are met` MEANS
    IF     `the Secretary of State has consulted the Governor of the Bank of England`
       AND `the Secretary of State is satisfied that, having regard to any undertaking given by the person with respect to any interest held or to be held by him in any shares, there are special reasons why that person should not be subject to the obligations imposed by section 793`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `Secretary of State`
         SHANT (`Action of a party` OF `Secretary of State`, Company, "s 796(2) grants an exemption from the operation of section 793")
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `Secretary of State` BECAUSE "s 796(2): an exemption was granted without the consultation and satisfaction the section requires"

§§ `s 797 Consequences of order imposing restrictions`

-- (1): the four effects of an order. Each function answers JUST TRUE where the effect applies. Under (4) the whole
-- section is "subject to" any direction under s 794(2) or s 799(3) and, for an interim order, to its terms: where the
-- act is within one, the effect does not apply (JUST FALSE, "subject to" read as an exception: see the fork register).
-- Where there is no order the text says nothing about the shares (NOTHING).
-- src:10813 | 797 Consequences of order imposing restrictions
-- src:10814 | (1) The effect of an order under section 794 that shares are subject to restrictions is as follows—
-- src:10815 | (a) any transfer of the shares is void;
-- src:10816 | (b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares;
-- src:10817 | (c) no further shares may be issued in right of the shares or in pursuance of an offer made to their holder;
-- src:10818 | (d) except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares, whether in respect of capital or otherwise.
@ref s 797(1)(a) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10813-10818)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(1)(a) any transfer of the shares is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effect of an order under section 794 that shares are subject to restrictions is as follows"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 797(1)(b) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10816-10816)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(1)(b) no voting rights are exercisable in respect of the shares` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effect of an order under section 794 that shares are subject to restrictions is as follows"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 797(1)(c) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10817-10817)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(1)(c) no further shares may be issued in right of the shares or in pursuance of an offer made to their holder` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effect of an order under section 794 that shares are subject to restrictions is as follows"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 797(1)(d) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10818-10818)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(1)(d) no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The effect of an order under section 794 that shares are subject to restrictions is as follows"
        IF `the payment is made in a liquidation` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) except in a liquidation, no payment may be made of sums due from the company on the shares"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2) and (3): the agreements that are void. "Where shares are subject to the restriction in ...": a "where" condition.
-- src:10819 | (2) Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(a), an agreement to transfer the shares is void.
-- src:10820 | This does not apply to an agreement to transfer the shares on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b) (removal of restrictions in case of court-approved transfer).
@ref s 797(2) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10819-10820)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is to transfer the shares on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(2) an agreement to transfer the shares is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(a)`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(a), an agreement to transfer the shares is void."
        IF `the agreement is to transfer the shares on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply to an agreement to transfer the shares on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:10821 | (3) Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(c) or (d), an agreement to transfer any right to be issued with other shares in right of those shares, or to receive any payment on them (otherwise than in a liquidation), is void.
-- src:10822 | This does not apply to an agreement to transfer any such right on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b) (removal of restrictions in case of court-approved transfer).
@ref s 797(3) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10821-10822)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is to transfer a right to be issued with other shares in right of those shares, or to receive a payment on them otherwise than in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is to transfer the right on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(3) an agreement to transfer any such right is void` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(c) or (d)`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where shares are subject to the restriction in subsection (1)(c) or (d), an agreement to transfer any right ... is void."
        IF (NOT `the agreement is to transfer a right to be issued with other shares in right of those shares, or to receive a payment on them otherwise than in a liquidation`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an agreement to transfer any right to be issued with other shares in right of those shares, or to receive any payment on them (otherwise than in a liquidation)": other agreements are not mentioned
        IF `the agreement is to transfer the right on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply to an agreement to transfer any such right on the making of an order under section 800 made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)"
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(4) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the "subject to" limit is applied inside each function above (inputs `the act is within a direction ...` and
-- `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order ...`).
-- src:10823 | (4) The provisions of this section are subject—
-- src:10824 | (a) to any directions under section 794(2) or section 799(3) (directions for protection of third parties), and
-- src:10825 | (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order.
@ref s 797(4) Consequences of order imposing restrictions (src:10823-10825)
GIVEN `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 797(4) the provisions of section 797 are displaced for the act` MEANS
    IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2) or section 799(3)` OR `the act is permitted by the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions ... (b) in the case of an interim order ..., to the terms of the order": an act within neither is not mentioned

§§ `s 798 Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions`

-- (1): "This section applies where ...".
-- src:10826 | 798 Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions
-- src:10827 | (1) This section applies where shares are subject to restrictions by virtue of an order under section 794.
@ref s 798(1) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10826-10827)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by virtue of an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the shares are subject to restrictions by virtue of an order under section 794`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where shares are subject to restrictions by virtue of an order under section 794."

-- (2): each limb is its own function; "the provisions of this section are subject to" any direction under s 794(2),
-- s 799 or s 800 and to the terms of an interim order (subsection (5)), taken as one input `the act is within a
-- direction or an interim order's terms`. "any such shares" in (b) and (a)(ii) is read as the shares of (a)(i): shares
-- that to the person's knowledge are subject to restrictions (fork register).
-- src:10828 | (2) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:10829 | (a) exercises or purports to exercise any right—
-- src:10830 | (i) to dispose of shares that to his knowledge, are for the time being subject to restrictions, or
-- src:10831 | (ii) to dispose of any right to be issued with any such shares, or
-- src:10832 | (b) votes in respect of any such shares (whether as holder or proxy), or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them, or
-- src:10833 | (c) being the holder of any such shares, fails to notify of their being subject to those restrictions a person whom he does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote in respect of those shares whether as holder or as proxy, or
-- src:10834 | (d) being the holder of any such shares, or being entitled to a right to be issued with other shares in right of them, or to receive any payment on them (otherwise than in a liquidation), enters into an agreement which is void under section 797(2) or (3).
@ref s 798(2)(a) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10828-10834)
GIVEN `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of a right to be issued with any such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(2)(a) the person commits an offence by exercising a right to dispose` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under— section 794(2) ..., or section 799 or 800 ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        IF `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` AND (   `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of shares` OR `the person exercises or purports to exercise a right to dispose of a right to be issued with any such shares`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person commits an offence if he— (a) exercises or purports to exercise any right— (i) to dispose of shares that to his knowledge, are for the time being subject to restrictions, or (ii) to dispose of any right to be issued with any such shares": a person who does none of the things listed is not mentioned

@ref s 798(2)(b) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10832-10832)
GIVEN `the person votes in respect of any such shares (whether as holder or proxy)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person appoints a proxy to vote in respect of any such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(2)(b) the person commits an offence by voting or appointing a proxy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under— section 794(2) ..., or section 799 or 800 ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        IF `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` AND (`the person votes in respect of any such shares (whether as holder or proxy)` OR `the person appoints a proxy to vote in respect of any such shares`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person commits an offence if he— ... (b) votes in respect of any such shares (whether as holder or proxy), or appoints a proxy to vote in respect of them": a person who does none of the things listed is not mentioned

@ref s 798(2)(c) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10833-10833)
GIVEN `the person is the holder of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to notify of their being subject to those restrictions another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does not know the other person to be aware of that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person does know the other person to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of those shares whether as holder or as proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(2)(c) the holder commits an offence by failing to notify the restrictions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under— section 794(2) ..., or section 799 or 800 ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        IF     `the person is the holder of the shares`
           AND `to the person's knowledge the shares are for the time being subject to restrictions`
           AND `the person fails to notify of their being subject to those restrictions another person`
           AND `the person does not know the other person to be aware of that fact`
           AND `the person does know the other person to be entitled, apart from the restrictions, to vote in respect of those shares whether as holder or as proxy`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person commits an offence if he— ... (c) being the holder of any such shares, fails to notify of their being subject to those restrictions a person whom he does not know to be aware of that fact but does know to be entitled (apart from the restrictions) to vote": a person who does none of the things listed is not mentioned

@ref s 798(2)(d) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10834-10834)
GIVEN `the person is the holder of any such shares or is entitled to a right to be issued with other shares in right of them, or to receive a payment on them otherwise than in a liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person enters into an agreement which is void under section 797(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(2)(d) the person commits an offence by entering into a void agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions under— section 794(2) ..., or section 799 or 800 ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order under section 794(3), to the terms of the order."
        IF `the person is the holder of any such shares or is entitled to a right to be issued with other shares in right of them, or to receive a payment on them otherwise than in a liquidation` AND `the person enters into an agreement which is void under section 797(2) or (3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person commits an offence if he— ... (d) being the holder of any such shares, or being entitled to a right to be issued with other shares in right of them, or to receive any payment on them (otherwise than in a liquidation), enters into an agreement which is void under section 797(2) or (3)": a person who does none of the things listed is not mentioned

-- (3): shares issued in contravention of the restrictions: an offence by the company and by every officer in default.
-- src:10835 | (3) If shares in a company are issued in contravention of the restrictions, an offence is committed by—
-- src:10836 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10837 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 798(3) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10835-10837)
GIVEN `shares in the company are issued in contravention of the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company are issued in contravention of the restrictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares in a company are issued in contravention of the restrictions, an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 798(3)(b) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10837-10837)
GIVEN `shares in the company are issued in contravention of the restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `shares in the company are issued in contravention of the restrictions`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares in a company are issued in contravention of the restrictions, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10838 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:10839 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:10840 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 798(4) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10838-10840)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 798(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                   daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment`                    THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`,                    NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`,                  NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`     THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`,     NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`              THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,              NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): every Mode of conviction is listed above

-- (5): "the provisions of this section are subject to" directions and the terms of an interim order: applied inside
