@ref s 798(5) Penalty for attempted evasion of restrictions (src:10841-10845)
GIVEN `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 798(5) the provisions of section 798 are displaced for the act` MEANS
    IF `the act is within a direction under section 794(2), 799 or 800 or the terms of an interim order under section 794(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of this section are subject— (a) to any directions ..., and (b) in the case of an interim order ..., to the terms of the order": an act within neither is not mentioned

§§ `s 799 Relaxation of restrictions`

-- src:10846 | 799 Relaxation of restrictions
-- src:10847 | (1) An application may be made to the court on the ground that an order directing that shares shall be subject to restrictions unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the shares.
@ref s 799(1) Relaxation of restrictions (src:10846-10847)
GIVEN `the ground of the application is that an order directing that shares shall be subject to restrictions unfairly affects the rights of third parties in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
