GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 799(2) the person may make an application for an order under section 799` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is aggrieved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made by the company or by any person aggrieved" does not say "only"

-- src:10849 | (3) If the court is satisfied that the application is well-founded, it may, for the purpose of protecting the rights of third parties in respect of the shares, and subject to such terms as it thinks fit, direct that such acts by such persons or descriptions of persons and for such purposes as may be set out in the order do not constitute a breach of the restrictions.
@ref s 799(3) Relaxation of restrictions (src:10849-10849)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the application is well-founded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 799(3) the court may direct that acts set out in the order do not constitute a breach of the restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the application is well-founded`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied that the application is well-founded, it may": a grant gated by if; the text is silent on the case where the gate fails (fork F44)

§§ `s 800 Removal of restrictions`

-- src:10850 | 800 Removal of restrictions
-- src:10851 | (1) An application may be made to the court for an order directing that the shares shall cease to be subject to restrictions.
@ref s 800(1) Removal of restrictions (src:10850-10851)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(1) an application may be made to the court for an order directing that the shares shall cease to be subject to restrictions` MEANS
    IF `the shares are subject to restrictions by an order under section 794`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of shares that are to "cease to be subject to restrictions" and says nothing of shares that are not

-- src:10852 | (2) An application for an order under this section may be made by the company or by any person aggrieved.
@ref s 800(2) Removal of restrictions (src:10852-10852)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is aggrieved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(2) the person may make an application for an order under section 800` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company` OR `the person is aggrieved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made by the company or by any person aggrieved" does not say "only"

-- (3): "must not make an order unless (a) or (b)": the bar. Whether the court is satisfied, and whether it approves, are
-- the court's judgments, so they are inputs.
-- src:10853 | (3) The court must not make an order under this section unless—
-- src:10854 | (a) it is satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company and no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure, or
-- src:10855 | (b) the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer.
@ref s 800(3) Removal of restrictions (src:10853-10855)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court approves the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(3) the court is barred from making an order under section 800` MEANS
    IF    (   `the court is satisfied that the relevant facts about the shares have been disclosed to the company`
           AND `the court is satisfied that no unfair advantage has accrued to any person as a result of the earlier failure to make that disclosure`)
       OR (   `the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration`
           AND `the court approves the transfer`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court must not make an order under this section unless— (a) it is satisfied that ... or (b) the shares are to be transferred for valuable consideration and the court approves the transfer": a condition is met, so the bar does not apply
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10856 | (4) An order under this section made by virtue of subsection (3)(b) may continue, in whole or in part, the restrictions mentioned in section 797(1)(c) and (d) (restrictions on issue of further shares or making of payments) so far as they relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer.
@ref s 800(4) Removal of restrictions (src:10856-10856)
GIVEN `the order is made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restrictions are those mentioned in section 797(1)(c) and (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restrictions relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(4) the order may continue the restrictions` MEANS
    IF     `the order is made by virtue of subsection (3)(b)`
       AND `the restrictions are those mentioned in section 797(1)(c) and (d)`
       AND `the restrictions relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order under this section made by virtue of subsection (3)(b) may continue, in whole or in part, the restrictions mentioned in section 797(1)(c) and (d) ... so far as they relate to a right acquired or offer made before the transfer"

-- src:10857 | (5) Where any restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)—
-- src:10858 | (a) an application may be made under this section for an order directing that the shares shall cease to be subject to those restrictions, and
-- src:10859 | (b) subsection (3) does not apply in relation to the making of such an order.
@ref s 800(5) Removal of restrictions (src:10857-10859)
GIVEN `restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(5)(a) an application may be made for an order directing that the shares shall cease to be subject to those restrictions` MEANS
    IF `restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)— (a) an application may be made under this section"

@ref s 800(5)(b) Removal of restrictions (src:10859-10859)
GIVEN `restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 800(5)(b) subsection (3) does not apply in relation to the making of such an order` MEANS
    IF `restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any restrictions continue in force under subsection (4)— ... (b) subsection (3) does not apply": where none continue, (b) is not engaged

§§ `s 801 Order for sale of shares`

-- src:10861 | (1) The court may order that the shares subject to restrictions be sold, subject to the court's approval as to the sale.
@ref s 801(1) Order for sale of shares (src:10861-10861)
GIVEN `the shares are subject to restrictions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 801(1) the court may order that the shares subject to restrictions be sold, subject to the court's approval as to the sale` MEANS
    IF `the shares are subject to restrictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may order that the shares subject to restrictions be sold"

-- src:10862 | (2) An application for an order under subsection (1) may only be made by the company.
@ref s 801(2) Order for sale of shares (src:10862-10862)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 801(2) the person may apply for an order under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the person is the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for an order under subsection (1) may only be made by the company."

-- src:10863 | (3) Where the court has made an order under this section, it may make such further order relating to the sale or transfer of the shares as it thinks fit.
@ref s 801(3) Order for sale of shares (src:10863-10863)
GIVEN `the court has made an order under section 801` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 801(3) the court may make such further order relating to the sale or transfer of the shares as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the court has made an order under section 801`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the court has made an order under this section, it may make such further order"

-- src:10864 | (4) An application for an order under subsection (3) may be made—
-- src:10865 | (a) by the company,
-- src:10866 | (b) by the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale, or
-- src:10867 | (c) by any person interested in the shares.
@ref s 801(4) Order for sale of shares (src:10864-10867)
GIVEN `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 801(4) the person may apply for an order under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF     `the person is the company`
        OR `the person is the person appointed by or in pursuance of the order to effect the sale`
        OR `the person is a person interested in the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made— (a) by the company, (b) by the person appointed ..., or (c) by any person interested in the shares" does not say "only"

-- src:10868 | (5) On making an order under subsection (1) or (3) the court may order that the applicant's costs (in Scotland, expenses) be paid out of the proceeds of sale.
@ref s 801(5) Order for sale of shares (src:10868-10868)
GIVEN `the court makes an order under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 801(5) the court may order that the applicant's costs (in Scotland, expenses) be paid out of the proceeds of sale` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order under subsection (1) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On making an order under subsection (1) or (3) the court may order that the applicant's costs ... be paid out of the proceeds of sale." ("on making" counts as "where")

§§ `s 802 Application of proceeds of sale under court order`

-- (1): the sum paid into court is the proceeds less the costs of the sale. Pounds are inputs.
-- src:10870 | (1) Where shares are sold in pursuance of an order of the court under section 801, the proceeds of the sale, less the costs of the sale, must be paid into court for the benefit of the persons who are beneficially interested in the shares.
@ref s 802(1) Application of proceeds of sale under court order (src:10870-10870)
GIVEN `the shares are sold in pursuance of an order of the court under section 801` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeds of the sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the costs of the sale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 802(1) the sum to be paid into court for the benefit of the persons who are beneficially interested in the shares` MEANS
    IF `the shares are sold in pursuance of an order of the court under section 801`
    THEN JUST (`the proceeds of the sale` MINUS `the costs of the sale`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where shares are sold in pursuance of an order of the court under section 801": the number is not defined elsewhere

-- src:10871 | (2) A person who is beneficially interested in the shares may apply to the court for the whole or part of those proceeds to be paid to him.
@ref s 802(2) Application of proceeds of sale under court order (src:10871-10871)
GIVEN `the person is beneficially interested in the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 802(2) the person may apply to the court for the whole or part of those proceeds to be paid to him` MEANS
    IF `the person is beneficially interested in the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is beneficially interested in the shares may apply"

-- (3): the amount the court shall order paid to the applicant. (a): the whole of the proceeds with interest;
-- (b): where another person had a beneficial interest at the time of the sale, the proportion that the value of the
-- applicant's interest bears to the total value of the shares, of the proceeds and interest.
-- src:10872 | (3) On such an application the court shall order the payment to the applicant of—
-- src:10873 | (a) the whole of the proceeds of sale together with any interest on them, or
-- src:10874 | (b) if another person had a beneficial interest in the shares at the time of their sale, such proportion of the proceeds and interest as the value of the applicant's interest in the shares bears to the total value of the shares.
-- src:10875 | This is subject to the following qualification.
@ref s 802(3) Application of proceeds of sale under court order (src:10872-10875)
GIVEN `the proceeds of sale` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest on them` IS A NUMBER
      `another person had a beneficial interest in the shares at the time of their sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the applicant's interest in the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the total value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 802(3) the amount the court shall order paid to the applicant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `another person had a beneficial interest in the shares at the time of their sale`) THEN JUST (`the proceeds of sale` PLUS `the interest on them`)
        IF `the total value of the shares` GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST ((`the proceeds of sale` PLUS `the interest on them`) TIMES (`the value of the applicant's interest in the shares` DIVIDED BY `the total value of the shares`))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a proportion of a total value of nothing is not defined by the text

-- (4): the qualification: where the court ordered costs out of the proceeds under s 801(5), the applicant under that
-- section is entitled to his costs out of the proceeds before any person interested in the shares receives any part.
-- src:10876 | (4) If the court has ordered under section 801(5) that the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of an applicant under that section are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale, the applicant is entitled to payment of his costs (or expenses) out of those proceeds before any person interested in the shares receives any part of those proceeds.
@ref s 802(4) Application of proceeds of sale under court order (src:10876-10876)
GIVEN `the court has ordered under section 801(5) that the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of an applicant under that section are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 802(4) the applicant under section 801 is entitled to payment of his costs out of the proceeds before any person interested in the shares receives any part` MEANS
    IF `the court has ordered under section 801(5) that the costs (in Scotland, expenses) of an applicant under that section are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court has ordered under section 801(5) that the costs ... of an applicant under that section are to be paid out of the proceeds of sale, the applicant is entitled to payment of his costs"

§§ `s 803 Power of members to require company to act`

-- src:10878 | 803 Power of members to require company to act
-- src:10879 | (1) The members of a company may require it to exercise its powers under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in shares).
@ref s 803(1) Power of members to require company to act (src:10878-10879)
GIVEN `the persons are members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 803(1) the persons may require the company to exercise its powers under section 793` MEANS
    IF `the persons are members of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a company may require it to exercise its powers": a person who is not a member is not mentioned

-- (2): the company is required once it has received requests to the same effect from members holding at least 10% of
-- the paid-up capital that carries a right to vote at general meetings (excluding the voting rights attached to
-- treasury shares). Amounts are pounds of paid-up capital: inputs.
-- src:10880 | (2) A company is required to do so once it has received requests (to the same effect) from members of the company holding at least 10% of such of the paid-up capital of the company as carries a right to vote at general meetings of the company (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares).
@ref s 803(2) Power of members to require company to act (src:10880-10880)
GIVEN `the requests received are to the same effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the paid-up capital carrying a right to vote at general meetings held by the members who made the requests` IS A NUMBER
      `the paid-up capital of the company carrying a right to vote at general meetings, excluding the voting rights attached to shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 803(2) the company is required to exercise its powers under section 793` MEANS
    IF     `the requests received are to the same effect`
       AND `the paid-up capital carrying a right to vote at general meetings held by the members who made the requests` AT LEAST (`the paid-up capital of the company carrying a right to vote at general meetings, excluding the voting rights attached to shares held as treasury shares` TIMES 10%)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is required to do so once it has received requests (to the same effect) from members of the company holding at least 10% of such of the paid-up capital": "once" is read as "where"

-- src:10881 | (3) A request—
-- src:10882 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form,
-- src:10883 | (b) must—
-- src:10884 | (i) state that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793,
-- src:10885 | (ii) specify the manner in which the company is requested to act, and
-- src:10886 | (iii) give reasonable grounds for requiring the company to exercise those powers in the manner specified, and
-- src:10887 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it.
@ref s 803(3) Power of members to require company to act (src:10881-10887)
GIVEN `the form of the request` IS A `Form of document`
      `the request states that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request specifies the manner in which the company is requested to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives reasonable grounds for requiring the company to exercise those powers in the manner specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 803(3) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    -- (a) "may be in hard copy form or in electronic form": both forms of the core's Form of document are allowed.
    IF     `the request states that the company is requested to exercise its powers under section 793`
       AND `the request specifies the manner in which the company is requested to act`
       AND `the request gives reasonable grounds for requiring the company to exercise those powers in the manner specified`
       AND `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A request ... (b) must— (i) state that the company is requested ..., (ii) specify the manner ..., and (iii) give reasonable grounds ..., and (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it": a requirement is not met, so the request does not meet them (the text does not say what follows)

§§ `s 804 Duty of company to comply with requirement`

-- src:10889 | (1) A company that is required under section 803 to exercise its powers under section 793 (notice requiring information about interests in company's shares) must exercise those powers in the manner specified in the requests.
@ref s 804(1) Duty of company to comply with requirement (src:10889-10889)
GIVEN `the company is required under section 803 to exercise its powers under section 793` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 804(1) the company must exercise those powers in the manner specified in the requests` MEANS
    IF `the company is required under section 803 to exercise its powers under section 793`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that is required under section 803 to exercise its powers under section 793 ... must exercise those powers in the manner specified in the requests." (read as an "if": marginal reading (a))

@ref s 804(1) Duty of company to comply with requirement (src:10889-10889)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 804(1) the company that is required under section 803 must exercise its powers in the manner specified` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Company, "s 804(1) exercises its powers under section 793 in the manner specified in the requests")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 804(1): the powers under section 793 were not exercised in the manner specified in the requests"

-- src:10890 | (2) If default is made in complying with subsection (1) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 804(2) Duty of company to comply with requirement (src:10890-10890)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 804(2) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with subsection (1)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with subsection (1) an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10891 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:10892 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:10893 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 804(3) Duty of company to comply with requirement (src:10891-10893)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 804(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                   daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment`                    THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`,                    NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`,                  NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`     THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`,     NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`              THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,              NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): every Mode of conviction is listed above

§§ `s 805 Report to members on outcome of investigation`

-- (1): the report must be made available within a reasonable period, not more than 15 days, after the conclusion of the
-- investigation. s 827: the 15 days are working days, so the count is of working days elapsed (an input the person states).
-- src:10895 | (1) On the conclusion of an investigation carried out by a company in pursuance of a requirement under section 803 the company must cause a report of the information received in pursuance of the investigation to be prepared.
-- src:10896 | The report must be made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the conclusion of the investigation.
@ref s 805(1) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10895-10896)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the conclusion of the investigation to the day the report was made available for inspection` IS A NUMBER
      `the period taken was a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(1) the report was made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the conclusion of the investigation` MEANS
    IF     `the period taken was a reasonable period`
       AND `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the conclusion of the investigation to the day the report was made available for inspection` AT MOST 15
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must be made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the conclusion of the investigation."

@ref s 805(1) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10895-10896)
GIVEN `the day on which the investigation concluded` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 805(1) the last day for making the report available for inspection` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the day on which the investigation concluded` 15 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

@ref s 805(1) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10895-10896)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 805(1) the company must make the report available for inspection after the conclusion of the investigation` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(1) makes the report available for inspection")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 805(1): the report was not made available for inspection within the period"

-- (2): an interim report for each period of three months of an investigation that runs on. The number due is the number of
-- three-month periods, counted from the day the company became subject to the requirement, that end before the
-- conclusion of the investigation ("not concluded within three months after the date", and each succeeding period
-- "ending before the conclusion").
-- src:10897 | (2) Where—
-- src:10898 | (a) a company undertakes an investigation in pursuance of a requirement under section 803, and
-- src:10899 | (b) the investigation is not concluded within three months after the date on which the company became subject to the requirement,
-- src:10900 | the company must cause to be prepared in respect of that period, and in respect of each succeeding period of three months ending before the conclusion of the investigation, an interim report of the information received during that period in pursuance of the investigation.
@ref s 805(2) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10897-10900)
GIVEN `the date on which the company became subject to the requirement` IS A DATE
      `the date of the conclusion of the investigation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 805(2) the number of interim reports the company must cause to be prepared` MEANS
    count 1
    WHERE
        GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A NUMBER
        count MEANS
            IF Day (`add months` `the date on which the company became subject to the requirement` (3 TIMES k)) LESS THAN Day `the date of the conclusion of the investigation`
            THEN 1 PLUS (count (k PLUS 1))
            ELSE 0

-- (3): each report must be made available within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the end of the
-- period to which it relates.
-- src:10901 | (3) Each such report must be made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the end of the period to which it relates.
@ref s 805(3) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10901-10901)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the end of the period to which the report relates to the day the report was made available for inspection` IS A NUMBER
      `the period taken was a reasonable period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(3) each such report was made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the end of the period to which it relates` MEANS
    IF     `the period taken was a reasonable period`
       AND `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the end of the period to which the report relates to the day the report was made available for inspection` AT MOST 15
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Each such report must be made available for inspection within a reasonable period (not more than 15 days) after the end of the period to which it relates."

@ref s 805(3) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10901-10901)
GIVEN `the last day of the period to which the report relates` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 805(3) the last day for making the report available for inspection` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the last day of the period to which the report relates` 15 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

-- (4): kept for at least six years from the date first made available, at the registered office or at a place specified in
-- regulations under s 1136 (a seam: an input).
-- src:10902 | (4) The reports must be retained by the company for at least six years from the date on which they are first made available for inspection and must be kept available for inspection during that time—
-- src:10903 | (a) at the company's registered office, or
-- src:10904 | (b) at a place specified in regulations under section 1136.
@ref s 805(4) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10902-10904)
GIVEN `the date on which the reports were first made available for inspection` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(4) the reports must still be retained and kept available for inspection` MEANS
    IF Day `the date on which the question is asked` AT MOST Day (`add years` `the date on which the reports were first made available for inspection` 6)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The reports must be retained by the company for at least six years from the date on which they are first made available for inspection": the six years have run out

@ref s 805(4) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10903-10904)
GIVEN `the reports are kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(4) the place at which the reports are kept is a place at which they must be kept available for inspection` MEANS
    IF `the reports are kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE `s 1136 the place is specified in regulations under section 1136` -- JUST FALSE is the seam's own no ("(b) a place specified in regulations under section 1136"); NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text)

-- (5): notice to the registrar of the place and of any change, unless the reports have at all times been kept at the
-- registered office.
-- src:10905 | (5) The company must give notice to the registrar—
-- src:10906 | (a) of the place at which the reports are kept available for inspection, and
-- src:10907 | (b) of any change in that place,
-- src:10908 | unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office.
@ref s 805(5) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10905-10908)
GIVEN `the reports have at all times been kept at the company's registered office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(5) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place and of any change in that place` MEANS
    IF `the reports have at all times been kept at the company's registered office`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless they have at all times been kept at the company's registered office"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 805(5) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10905-10908)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 805(5) the company must give notice to the registrar of the place at which the reports are kept` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Registrar, "s 805(5) gives notice of the place at which the reports are kept available for inspection and of any change in that place")
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 805(5): notice of the place of the reports was not given to the registrar"

-- src:10909 | (6) The company must within three days of making any report prepared under this section available for inspection, notify the members who made the requests under section 803 where the report is so available.
@ref s 805(6) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10909-10909)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from making the report available for inspection to notifying the members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(6) the company notified the members who made the requests where the report is available within three days` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from making the report available for inspection to notifying the members` AT MOST 3
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must within three days of making any report prepared under this section available for inspection, notify the members who made the requests under section 803 where the report is so available."

@ref s 805(6) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10909-10909)
GIVEN `the day on which the report was made available for inspection` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 805(6) the last day for notifying the members who made the requests` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the day on which the report was made available for inspection` 3 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

@ref s 805(6) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10909-10909)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 805(6) the company must notify the members who made the requests where the report is available` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 805(6) notifies the members who made the requests where the report is available for inspection")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 805(6): the members were not notified within three days"

-- (7): the investigation is concluded when the company has made all necessary or expedient inquiries and, for each
-- inquiry, a response has been received or the time allowed has elapsed.
DECLARE `s 805(7) inquiry` HAS
    `s 805(7)(b)(i) a response has been received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 805(7)(b)(ii) the time allowed for a response has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:10910 | (7) For the purposes of this section an investigation carried out by a company in pursuance of a requirement under section 803 is concluded when—
-- src:10911 | (a) the company has made all such inquiries as are necessary or expedient for the purposes of the requirement, and
-- src:10912 | (b) in the case of each such inquiry—
-- src:10913 | (i) a response has been received by the company, or
-- src:10914 | (ii) the time allowed for a response has elapsed.
@ref s 805(7) Report to members on outcome of investigation (src:10910-10914)
GIVEN `the company has made all such inquiries as are necessary or expedient for the purposes of the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      inquiries IS A LIST OF `s 805(7) inquiry`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 805(7) the investigation carried out by the company in pursuance of a requirement under section 803 is concluded` MEANS
    IF     `the company has made all such inquiries as are necessary or expedient for the purposes of the requirement`
       AND all (GIVEN i YIELD i's `s 805(7)(b)(i) a response has been received by the company` OR i's `s 805(7)(b)(ii) the time allowed for a response has elapsed`) inquiries
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an investigation ... is concluded when— (a) the company has made all such inquiries ..., and (b) in the case of each such inquiry— (i) a response has been received by the company, or (ii) the time allowed for a response has elapsed" ("when" read as "where")

§§ `s 806 Report to members: offences`

-- src:10916 | (1) If default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5) (notice to registrar of place at which reports made available for inspection) an offence is committed by—
-- src:10917 | (a) the company, and
-- src:10918 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 806(1) Report to members: offences (src:10916-10918)
GIVEN `default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5) ... an offence is committed by— (a) the company"

@ref s 806(1)(b) Report to members: offences (src:10918-10918)
GIVEN `default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made for 14 days in complying with section 805(5) ... an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10919 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 806(2) Report to members: offences (src:10919-10919)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 806(2) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                           daily default fine,                                                    imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`  THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,  NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1), JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1), FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says only "on summary conviction"; a conviction on indictment is not mentioned

-- src:10920 | (3) If default is made in complying with any other provision of section 805 (report to members on outcome of investigation), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 806(3) Report to members: offences (src:10920-10920)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with a provision of section 805 other than section 805(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 806(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with a provision of section 805 other than section 805(5)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default` -- JUST FALSE here is the text's "who is in default"; NOTHING stays NOTHING (points outside the text, s 1121)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with any other provision of section 805 ..., an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default."

-- src:10921 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable—
-- src:10922 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:10923 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 806(4) Report to members: offences (src:10921-10923)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 806(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    --                         how convicted,                imprisonment not exceeding, fine not exceeding,                                   daily default fine, imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment`                    THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`,                    NOTHING, JUST `a fine without a stated limit`,                  NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction`                          THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`,                          NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales`     THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`,     NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland`              THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`,              NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`      THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`,      NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): every Mode of conviction is listed above

§§ `s 807 Right to inspect and request copy of reports`

-- src:10925 | (1) Any report prepared under section 805 must be open to inspection by any person without charge.
@ref s 807(1) Right to inspect and request copy of reports (src:10925-10925)
GIVEN `the report was prepared under section 805` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 807(1) the report must be open to inspection by any person without charge` MEANS
    IF `the report was prepared under section 805`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any report prepared under section 805 must be open to inspection by any person without charge." (a report not prepared under section 805 is outside the subsection)

-- src:10926 | (2) Any person is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy of any such report or any part of it.
-- src:10927 | The copy must be provided within ten days after the request is received by the company.
@ref s 807(2) Right to inspect and request copy of reports (src:10926-10927)
GIVEN `the person has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 807(2) the person is entitled to be provided with a copy of the report or any part of it` MEANS
    IF `the person has made a request` AND `the person has paid such fee as may be prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person is entitled, on request and on payment of such fee as may be prescribed, to be provided with a copy" ("on" counts as "where")

@ref s 807(2) Right to inspect and request copy of reports (src:10927-10927)
GIVEN `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the day the request was received by the company to the day the copy was provided` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 807(2) the copy was provided within ten days after the request was received` MEANS
    IF `the number of working days, reckoned under section 827, from the day the request was received by the company to the day the copy was provided` AT MOST 10
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The copy must be provided within ten days after the request is received by the company."

@ref s 807(2) Right to inspect and request copy of reports (src:10927-10927)
GIVEN `the day on which the request was received by the company` IS A DATE
      `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company` IS A FUNCTION FROM DATE TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 807(2) the last day for providing the copy` MEANS
    `s 827 the last day of a period of days counting only working days` `the day on which the request was received by the company` 10 `s 1173(1) the day is a working day for the company`

@ref s 807(2) Right to inspect and request copy of reports (src:10927-10927)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 807(2) the company must provide the copy after the request is received` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST (`Action of a party` OF Company, Member, "s 807(2) provides the person with a copy of the report or part of it")
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed, reckoned under section 827`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 807(2): the copy was not provided within ten days after the request was received"

